lti-agent reasoning + confidence gate on natural-language decisions\nAI-Factory  | Produces products; optionally calls Metis on high-stakes stages (`architect`, `methodologist`)\nARGUS  | Demand-side agent; can consume Metis + MCP tools like any other host\n\nHard invariant: factory and Metis are independent. Missing Metis → factory runs unchanged (fail-open gate). Missing factory → Metis serves `/v1/*` normally.\n\n## Factory integration (optional gate)\n\nHigh-stakes pipeline stages can POST to Metis `/v1/verify` via `llm/metis_gate.py` (HTTP only — never imports `metis`).\n    \n    `export METIS_URL=https://metis.internal:8080   # default http://127.0.0.1:8080\n    export AIFACTORY_METIS_GATE=auto               # auto | on | off (default auto)\n    export AIFACTORY_METIS_GATE_BLOCK=0          # 1 = allow low-confidence to escalate\n    `\n\nFull env table + sequence diagrams: `docs/metis-integration.md` · RU · ES · FR · ZH\n\n## MCP tools (Metis as consumer)\n\nMetis agents can attach ecosystem MCP servers via presets:\n\nPreset  | Server  | Tools\n--- | --- | ---\n`aimarket-oracle-gateway`  | aimarket-oracle-gateway  | 35 verifiable oracle tools\n`aimarket-web`  | aimarket-mcp  | `web_fetch`, `web_search`, `metis_verify` (SSRF-hardened)\n    \n    `enable_mcp_tools: true\n    mcp_ecosystem_presets:\n      - aimarket-oracle-gateway\n      - aimarket-web\n    `\n\naimarket-mcp — shared MCP gateway (stdio on Glama, HTTP self-host). Written once; consumed by Metis, ARGUS, and any stdio/HTTP MCP host.\n\nMetis-side doc: `metis/docs/en/ECOSYSTEM.md`\n\n## Alien Monitor\n\nMetis appears as the `cognition` node in Alien Monitor — live stats + in-graph chat proxied server-side (`POST /api/metis/chat`) so API keys never reach the browser.\n\n## Quick start (standalone)\n    \n    `git clone https://github.com/alexar76/metis.git && cd metis\n    pip install -e \".[dev,distributed]\"\n    metis-serve --port 8080\n    # OpenAPI: /v1/verify · /v1/chat/completions · /aimarket/invoke\n    `\n\nDocker: `docker compose up -d` in the metis repo.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTHEMIS — Admit. Or don’t. Before the catalogue. (https://alexar76.github.io/themis/)\nciteturn28search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; $ `uvx create-aimarket-agent themis --kind tool --metis` [Button: COPY] ... capability `agent.security.supply-chain.audit@v1` MIT · a procurement aid, not a compliance certification alexar76.github.io/themis\n\nAIMarket · publish admission\n\n# Admit. Or don’t.\nBefore the catalogue.\n\nTHEMIS (Θέμις) is the signed publish-time gate: `approve` / `review` / `reject` from a bounded dossier — deterministic policy, request-bound Ed25519 receipt, no free crawl of the candidate. Not Metis (cognition). Not WARDEN (invoke-time firewall).\n\nSee it on Alien Monitor Open the console Rebuild from the mini-course\n\n$ `uvx create-aimarket-agent themis --kind tool --metis` [Button: COPY]\n\nAPPROVE catalogue path\n\nREVIEW human · Metis advisory\n\nREJECT fail closed\n\nWebGL is unavailable here. The gate logic is identical — read the signed verdicts below.\n\n3\n\nVerdicts\n\n84\n\nTests\n\n98%\n\nCoverage\n\nEd25519\n\nSigned receipt\n\n12\n\nCourse steps\n\n5\n\nLanguages\n\nCandidate → gate → receipt\n\n## One dossier in. One signed verdict out.\n\nThe policy engine decides immediately from identity, transport, permissions, cost, schemas and evidence shape. Metis may add an asynchronous second opinion — it never overrides the signed verdict. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nARGUS 3 MCP Server: MCP server, setup and security (https://info-agent-ia.com/en/mcp/alexar76-argus/)\nciteturn28search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: last week; ARGUS 3 MCP Server is an open-source MCP server published on GitHub that lets an AI agent query ARGUS-3 and assess third-party MCP servers through WARDEN. ... Created on June 23, 2026, the ale